 166:source\asw/main.c **** /**
 167:source\asw/main.c ****  * \brief Program entry point: enable the interrupts, start the system tick and the OS.
 168:source\asw/main.c ****  *
 169:source\asw/main.c ****  * Sets the system tick period to 1 ms (derived from the bus clock BCLK__BUS_CLK__HZ),
 170:source\asw/main.c ****  * enables its interrupt and starts it, then hands over to the operating system.
 171:source\asw/main.c ****  * StartOS() does not return; the endless loop below it is a safety net only (N7).
 172:source\asw/main.c ****  * The first task that runs is tsk_init.
 173:source\asw/main.c ****  *
 174:source\asw/main.c ****  * \return does not return (int by the C standard)
 175:source\asw/main.c ****  * \note   Signature "int main()" is kept as it is (N8).
 176:source\asw/main.c ****  */
